QwzAirport.kext: credits and what comes from where

QwzAirport is the native Wi-Fi front of QwzWifi (docs/native-wifi-research.md §8.5, §8.8).
It is GPL-2.0, like kext/. It starts from the native front of laobamac/itlwm, commit
738d4c61b5a64433b27c1ab09dba94916ab77d8d (https://github.com/laobamac/itlwm, GPL-2.0),
itself based on AirportItlwm by zxystd and the OpenIntelWireless contributors
(https://github.com/OpenIntelWireless/itlwm). Everything here, ABI headers and WCL.hpp
included, is our copy: later fixes in the fork are reviewed and ported by hand
(abi/UPSTREAM says how to diff against it).

Taken, and from which file of laobamac/itlwm 738d4c6:
- abi/Airport/: IO80211/Skywalk/CoreCapture headers from include/Airport/ (Tahoe subset);
  our changes are marked QWZAIRPORT/QWZMAC.
  apple80211_var.h, apple80211_ioctl.h are Apple's (APSL headers, as published).
  The headers are trusted only after scripts/kc-abi.py --check on the running build.
- WCL.hpp: AirportItlwm/WCL/WCL.hpp, unmodified (message ids and layouts, request decoders).
- QwzAirport.cpp/.hpp: from AirportItlwm/AirportItlwmV2.cpp/.hpp (work queue, CoreCapture
  pipes and fault reporter, interface setup, capability bits). Without the PCI, power
  management and itlwm HAL parts: QwzWifi owns the device.
- QwzAirportInterface.cpp/.hpp: from AirportItlwm/AirportItlwmSkywalkInterface.cpp/.hpp and
  WCL/WCL.cpp (lifecycle messages, state and channel requests). Their net80211 accesses are
  replaced by calls through kext/airport_api.h, implemented by QwzWifi over OpenBSD net80211.
- QwzAirportEthernet.cpp/.hpp: from AirportItlwm/AirportItlwmEthernetInterface.cpp/.hpp,
  largely unchanged.

Ours: kext/airport_api.h and its implementation in kext/QwzWifi.cpp, adapter/'s
qwzmac_qwz_channels()/qwzmac_qwz_country()/radio callback, QWZMAC patches in qwz,
scripts/airport-stubs.py (QwzAirportStubs.inc), scripts/kc-abi.py,
scripts/kclib.py.

MAC reconfiguration / deferred-join ordering was compared with
mnnobre/AirportMtkWlan b880d9cd155ba076ae86dc02556f215fd82723d5
(AirportItlwmV2.cpp and WCL/WCL.cpp), itself based on laobamac/itlwm.
https://github.com/mnnobre/AirportMtkWlan

Airport-only firmware vdev MAC recreation follows the command/acknowledgement
ordering in Linux ath12k/mac.c (ath12k_mac_vdev_delete) and ath12k/wmi.c
(ath12k_wmi_vdev_delete, ath12k_vdev_delete_resp_event), adapted to qwz's
existing WMI transport and persistent DMA mappings. The ordinary HeliPort
association path is not replaced.

The macOS26 EXTENDED_BSS_INFO response layout follows AirportMtkWlan
copyWCLExtendedBss (same b880d9c reference above), using qwz/net80211's
actual negotiated data. ifnet uniqueid separation uses the public IOKit
initIfnetParams override described by Apple IONetworkingFamily.

Beacon supervision and native join ordering follow the WCL handlers in
laobamac/itlwm 738d4c6 and AirportMtkWlan b880d9c: actual associated-beacon
deltas in LqmUpdate, RSSI quality on change, and ordinary SCAN-based join.
Every eighth real associated beacon queues a counted seam event; QwzAirport
then snapshots RX and posts WCL in its gate, outside the net80211 spl lock. No synthetic beacon
heartbeat or unconditional stop/init is part of the join path.

Current-channel, RSSI and rate getter behavior follows the same pinned
AirportItlwmSkywalkInterface.cpp in laobamac/itlwm and AirportMtkWlan.
QwzCurrentLink translates qwz's actual status through the seam instead of
accessing their HAL/net80211 objects from the native front.

Early scan result publication follows both references' IEEE80211_EVT_BEACON
-> publishWCLBeacon path while scanPending, with separate SCAN_DONE. Our
cross-kext seam uses bounded 250 ms progress snapshots of actual ticketed RX
rather than calling WCL from the OpenBSD receive context.

The Tahoe INFRA_ENUMERATED availability replay and early BSD Wi-Fi subtype
publication are Qwz-specific fixes, not behavior copied from either pinned
reference. Those references leave INFRA_ENUMERATED unsupported and set the
BSD subtype during attachment. Placement and event routing were checked
against this Mac's 25G241 kernel collection.
